The ebusd client (src/ebusd/) was written in JavaScript for this project, from
the documentation of the TCP commands of ebusd in the ebusd wiki
(https://github.com/john30/ebusd/wiki, "3.1. TCP client commands") and from the
answers of the official ebusd 26.1 Docker image (john30/ebusd). The useful
message names and the unit to device class mapping take their inspiration from
the Home Assistant MQTT configuration shipped with ebusd
(contrib/etc/ebusd/mqtt-hassio.cfg). No code was copied: ebusd and its
configuration files (john30/ebusd-configuration) are released under the GNU
General Public License v3.0, and the integration only talks to ebusd over the
network.

The test fixtures (test/fixtures/ebusd-26.1-*) are answers of ebusd 26.1 to
the "info" and "find" commands, built by ebusd from the ebusd-configuration
files for a Vaillant BAI00 boiler (GPL-3.0, quoted for interoperability
testing), completed by a few VRC 700 definitions written from
src/vaillant/15.700.tsp of ebusd-configuration.

